From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - reject skcipher lengths the hardware cannot process

The SPU-M does not report a request length it cannot process. ECB and
CBC requests with a partial last block complete with a good status, so
the self-tests report "unexpectedly succeeded", and requests the
software implementations reject reach the hardware.

Check the length first, as the software implementations do:
- ECB and CBC need whole blocks.
- XTS needs at least one block.
Complete an empty request at once instead of sending an empty message.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -1712,13 +1712,29 @@ cb_finish:
  */
 static int skcipher_enqueue(struct skcipher_request *req, bool encrypt)
 {
+	struct crypto_skcipher *tfm = crypto_skcipher_reqtfm(req);
 	struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx = skcipher_request_ctx(req);
-	struct iproc_ctx_s *ctx =
-	    crypto_skcipher_ctx(crypto_skcipher_reqtfm(req));
+	struct iproc_ctx_s *ctx = crypto_skcipher_ctx(tfm);
 	int err;
 
 	flow_log("%s() enc:%u\n", __func__, encrypt);
 
+	switch (ctx->cipher.mode) {
+	case CIPHER_MODE_ECB:
+	case CIPHER_MODE_CBC:
+		if (!IS_ALIGNED(req->cryptlen, crypto_skcipher_blocksize(tfm)))
+			return -EINVAL;
+		break;
+	case CIPHER_MODE_XTS:
+		if (req->cryptlen < AES_BLOCK_SIZE)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		break;
+	default:
+		break;
+	}
+	if (!req->cryptlen)
+		return 0;
+
 	rctx->gfp = (req->base.flags & (CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_BACKLOG |
 		       CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_SLEEP)) ? GFP_KERNEL : GFP_ATOMIC;
 	rctx->parent = &req->base;
